From 21cc893b91b33468ace14f49f544d26c153b6fc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tstoltz <tristan.stoltz@evolvingresonantcocreationism.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 19:31:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add Model S (persistent Unix-socket observation service; Nix
 owns native policy)

Wires nix-signature-verify-raw-daemon (a prototype persistent service,
see nix-signature-policy repo) into pathInfoIsUntrusted, structurally
identical to Model O-process's B+P composition but with a socket-connect
caller (signature-service-caller.{hh,cc}) instead of a fork/exec caller
-- no pipes, no reader/writer/waiter threads, just connect+write+
shutdown(SHUT_WR)+bounded-poll-read+close. Reuses Model N's
KeyGroup/allSignatureGroupsSatisfied policy composition, same as
O-process and O-provider.

New settings: signature-observation-service-{socket,mode,timeout-ms,
key-groups}. A misconfigured/absent/hung/malformed-response service is
always a hard refusal in conjunctive mode, never a silent pass --
verified end-to-end, not just asserted (see E2E scenarios below).

617/617 libstore-tests + 707/707 libutil-tests pass (no regressions).
Real E2E, 6/6 scenarios (measurement/run-models-e2e.sh): legacy never
connects; conjunctive admits when the service verifies a satisfied
group; a SECOND decision against the same already-running daemon
process also admits correctly (persistence itself exercised, not just
asserted); conjunctive refuses on an unsatisfiable group; a missing/
not-running service fails closed; a service that accepts a connection
but never responds correctly times out (~1080ms against a configured
1000ms deadline) and fails closed, rather than hanging Nix
indefinitely -- unlike O-provider, which has no timeout mechanism at
all for an in-process hang.
